# Design Primitives

## Package
`com.vitran.shop.ui.components` — `VitranText`, `VitranIcon`

## Prefer wrappers
- Use `VitranText` / `VitranIcon` for app chrome and repeated UI copy/icons.
- Roles: `VitranTextStyle` (`Headline`, `Title`, `Body`, `Label`) → Material typography slots.
- Icon defaults: `VitranSize.iconMedium`, tint `onSurface` (override via params).

```kotlin
// ✅ GOOD
VitranText(text = title, style = VitranTextStyle.Headline)
VitranIcon(painter = painter, contentDescription = label)

// ❌ BAD (repeated chrome)
Text(text = title, style = MaterialTheme.typography.headlineMedium)
Icon(painter = painter, contentDescription = label, modifier = Modifier.size(24.dp))
```

## Use raw Text / Icon when the need diverges
Keep Material `Text` / `Icon` when the wrapper does not fit, for example:
- Branded logo / asset with `Color.Unspecified` tint
- Custom `TextStyle` not represented by `VitranTextStyle`
- Annotated / multi-style strings
- One-off illustration icons with non-standard sizing/tinting

## Extending
- Add a `VitranTextStyle` role only when reuse across screens is likely.
- Prefer `VitranIcon(size = VitranSize.…)` over new icon wrappers for size variants.
- Do not invent parallel colors/sizes inside primitives — use theme + design tokens.
